Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(links): read links typed by the user (SSRF-guarded)
 and give them to the model as untrusted data

- src/links.js: URL extraction, SSRF guard (private/loopback/link-local/reserved IPv4+IPv6, obfuscated IPs, internal hosts, creds, ports, own host),
  manual redirects re-validated per hop (max 3), 8s timeout, 1MB download cap, 6000 chars/page, max 3 links
- page text wrapped in <web_page> blocks with angle brackets neutralised; system prompt: untrusted data, never follow, admit unread links
- multi-agent: researcher and writer passes receive the pages; page text is never stored in D1
- a message with links costs +1 daily unit; reply includes links[] and the UI lists links read/failed
- capability notice updated (still no search/files/code execution)
- tests: unit (extraction, SSRF matrix, redirects, size/time caps) + end-to-end on real SQLite + browser
